cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using this metadata and cite the underlying methodological sources listed in NOTICE.md."
title: "SPAN: Spending Priorities for Active Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Welch
    given-names: Tim
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/squirmen/spending-priorities-active-networks"
url: "https://span.tfwelch.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An open research tool that ranks possible new cycling links in Auckland, New
  Zealand, and puts them in a build order for a goal and a budget. It shows what
  each link would add, what it costs and how firm the estimate is, and checks
  which upgrades must be built together to complete a journey. Versions up to
  1.0 were released as the Auckland Cycling Investment Workbench.
keywords:
  - cycling
  - active transport
  - transport planning
  - investment prioritisation
  - network connectivity
  - Auckland
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The Propensity to Cycle Tool: An open source online system for sustainable transport planning"
    doi: "10.5198/jtlu.2016.862"
  - type: article
    title: "Scenarios of cycling to school in England, and associated health and carbon impacts"
    doi: "10.1016/j.jth.2019.01.008"
